; Game start and main loop
;
; Starts a game and then runs it: the code never returns, the Game Over screen and the ending jump back to $85FC.
; .
; Start. On a 48K machine ($8506 = 1) it draws the title screen script #R$A526; the first start enters at #R$8606
; instead (#R$6000 jumps there), because the loader's picture is already the title. It installs #R$A43D, the frame
; routine of the menus, in #R$8504, starts the title music (track 3; on a 128K #R$605F turns the LD HL at #R$860C into
; CALL #R$85F3), clears the 60 bytes $8512-$854D (respawn position, flags of the items and checkpoints, lives, crosses),
; sets 9 lives, enables the redraw of the lives bar and the crosses counter (#R$9BF3, #R$9C1B: a NOP written over their
; RET), and waits in the title menu for ENTER (#R$A339). It then installs the game frame routine #R$85E2, clears the
; exit direction and the room state, runs the intro, room 0, until a key is pressed (#R$8832), makes Jean stand
; (state 4), takes the respawn position and room from the checkpoint rules (#R$BDF3: with no checkpoint taken, room 5
; at X $2400, Y $4400, observed) and enters the room. On a 128K machine the title script is not drawn at all (by
; reading the code: the DEC A / CALL Z test is for a 48K machine only).
; .
; Main loop (#R$8664). The low 7 bits of the room state #R$850C say what to do, bit 7 only tells the frame routine
; #R$A596 to run the game logic:
; .
; 1 enter the room #R$8509: #R$86B9, then #R$9B5A draws it with a sweep, then the state becomes $80 (playing).
; .
; 2 respawn: copy the respawn position (#R$8512, #R$8514) to Jean's X and Y (#R$A8A1, #R$A8A3), then as 1.
; .
; 3 the ending: #R$887B, then start again at #R$85FC.
; .
; 4 after a death: #R$BDF3 chooses the checkpoint (room, position, state 0), then as 2.
; .
; 5 Game Over: script #R$A57E, music track 7, wait for a key, start again at #R$85FC.
; .
; anything else (0 with bit 7 set): one frame of play, see below.
; .
; One frame of play. The game logic does not run here but in the interrupt, once per frame at 50 Hz (#R$85E2 and
; #R$A596; observed: 800 interrupts and 800 game frames in frames 700-1500 of tests/inputs/play.txt). The loop below is
; the foreground, which only draws. It calls the four one-shot gates (#R$9CE7 event script, #R$9C51 parchment, #R$9BF3
; lives bar, #R$9C1B crosses counter: each is a RET until something arms it) over and over until the interrupt has
; completed a frame list (#R$BDDA is NOP, written by #R$A5DB), then runs the list of queued sprite commands (#R$BDDB),
; builds and draws the changed cells and sprites (#R$97B7, #R$95FF), steps the three tile animations (#R$AD88 water
; strip, #R$AE20 blood tiles, #R$AE4B ring of crosses; each a RET until a room script enables it) and tests the room
; state again. A quiet frame is drawn by about T 55,000 of the frame; a busy one takes the whole frame or more. When the
; drawing outlasts the next interrupt, that frame's game logic still runs but its sprites are not queued, so the screen
; is updated on fewer frames than the logic (observed, same run: 586 draws for 800 frames).
; .
; Hardware: none directly. The pacing comes from the gate #R$BDDA that the 50 Hz interrupt opens; the screen is written by
; the routines called from here.
@label=StartGame
c$85FC LD A,($8506)         ; machine type: 1 on a 48K Spectrum
 $85FF LD HL,$A526          ; title screen script
 $8602 DEC A                ; Z on a 48K machine
 $8603 CALL Z,$9D5F         ; RunScript: draw the title (48K only)
@label=StartGame_NoTitle
 $8606 LD HL,$A43D          ; first start enters here; menu frame routine for the title
 $8609 LD ($8504),HL        ; InterruptRoutine
@label=StartGame_Music
 $860C LD HL,$85F3          ; 128K: becomes CALL $85F3 (start the music), written by #R$605F; on a 48K it only loads HL
@isub=LD A,MUSIC_TRACK_TITLE
 $860F LD A,$03
 $8611 LD ($8551),A         ; MusicTrack
 $8614 LD HL,$8512          ; first byte to clear: RespawnX
 $8617 LD BC,$3C00          ; B = 60 bytes ($8512-$854D), C = 0
@label=StartGame_Clear
*$861A LD (HL),C
 $861B INC HL
 $861C DJNZ $861A
 $861E LD HL,$854D          ; Crosses: 0 (already cleared by the loop)
 $8621 LD (HL),C
 $8622 DEC HL
@isub=LD (HL),MAX_LIVES
 $8623 LD (HL),$09          ; Lives
 $8625 LD HL,$9C1B          ; DrawCrossesHud: NOP instead of RET, so it draws once
 $8628 LD (HL),C
 $8629 LD HL,$9BF3          ; DrawLivesBar: NOP instead of RET
 $862C LD (HL),C
 $862D LD HL,$A895          ; Jean's animation timer #R$A895
 $8630 LD (HL),$08
 $8632 CALL $A339           ; title menu: ENTER starts, C opens the controls menu
 $8635 LD HL,$85E2          ; game frame routine
 $8638 LD ($8504),HL
 $863B XOR A                ; exit direction 0 (right)
 $863C LD ($850B),A
 $863F LD ($850C),A         ; room state 0
 $8642 CALL $8832           ; intro: room 0 until a key is pressed
@isub=LD A,PLAYER_STANDING
 $8645 LD A,$04
 $8647 LD ($A894),A         ; PlayerState
@label=MainLoop_AfterDeath
*$864A CALL $BDF3           ; chooses room and respawn position, sets room state 0
@label=MainLoop_Respawn
*$864D LD HL,($8512)        ; respawn position X (8.8) ...
 $8650 LD ($A8A1),HL        ; ... to Jean's X
 $8653 LD HL,($8514)        ; respawn position Y ...
 $8656 LD ($A8A3),HL        ; ... to Jean's Y
@label=MainLoop_EnterRoom
*$8659 CALL $86B9           ; build the room
 $865C CALL $9B5A           ; draw it, sweeping in from the side Jean left by
@isub=LD A,STATE_RUNNING
 $865F LD A,$80
 $8661 LD ($850C),A         ; RoomState: playing
@label=MainLoop
*$8664 LD A,($850C)         ; RoomState
 $8667 AND $7F              ; bit 7 is only the "run the game logic" flag
 $8669 DEC A                ; state 1: enter the room
 $866A JR Z,$8659
 $866C DEC A                ; state 2: respawn
 $866D JR Z,$864D
 $866F DEC A                ; state 3: the ending
 $8670 JR Z,$869F
 $8672 DEC A                ; state 4: restart after a death
 $8673 JR Z,$864A
 $8675 DEC A                ; state 5: Game Over
 $8676 JR Z,$86A5
@label=MainLoop_Play
*$8678 CALL $9CE7           ; event script (once, when armed)
 $867B CALL $9C51           ; parchment (when one was picked up)
 $867E CALL $9BF3           ; lives bar
 $8681 CALL $9C1B           ; crosses counter
 $8684 LD A,($BDDA)         ; frame list gate: $C9 (RET) until the interrupt completes a list, then NOP
 $8687 OR A
 $8688 JR NZ,$8678          ; not ready: the gates again
 $868A CALL $BDDA           ; = #R$BDDB, run the frame list of sprite commands
 $868D CALL $97B7           ; build the redraw runs, draw the sprite jobs into the cells
 $8690 CALL $95FF           ; copy the cells to the screen
 $8693 CALL $AD88           ; water strip of rooms 16 and 19
 $8696 CALL $AE20           ; blood tiles of rooms 21-23
 $8699 CALL $AE4B           ; ring of crosses of room 24
 $869C JP $8664             ; next frame
@label=MainLoop_Ending
*$869F CALL $887B           ; the ending, then restart the game
 $86A2 JP $85FC
@label=MainLoop_GameOver
*$86A5 LD HL,$A57E          ; Game Over screen script
 $86A8 CALL $9D5F
@isub=LD A,MUSIC_TRACK_GAME_OVER
 $86AB LD A,$07             ; MusicTrack 7
 $86AD LD ($8551),A
 $86B0 CALL $A1C3           ; wait for a key press
 $86B3 CALL $A1CE           ; wait for the key to be released
 $86B6 JP $85FC
